inodune (0.1.11) stable; urgency=high

  * Security: a private-key header protects package documentation too
    (README, CHANGELOG, docs, wheel METADATA).
  * Group-writable evidence (Ubuntu umask 002) is accepted only for the
    user's private group; o+w and shared groups stay refused.
  * Hardlinks moved together to the Trash no longer block analyses; refusals
    list their reasons and --review ignores issues outside its target.
  * Bounded stored reports for very large cleanups; Portuguese dialog
    buttons; readable plan text; man pages.

 -- Caio Barbieri <70986039+caiolombello@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000

inodune (0.1.10) stable; urgency=high

  * Security: credentials detected by content (private-key headers, npm
    _authToken, AWS secret keys, netrc passwords) stay protected in every
    cleanup target, for Trash and permanent cleanup; files are re-checked
    right before they are moved or removed.
  * CLI: --review accepts node.modules; readable output without "/./".
  * Package: changelog next to copyright; SHA256SUMS lists present files.

 -- Caio Barbieri <70986039+caiolombello@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

inodune (0.1.9) stable; urgency=medium

  * UX review: low-risk items come pre-selected, cleanup button shows count
    and size, confirmations open as focused dialogs near the action.
  * Uninstall plans show friendly name, version, dependencies and size;
    PackageKit and polkit failures get specific messages.
  * Apps & Games: search, source/protection/size filters and an "N of M"
    counter.
  * Backend: deduplicated PackageKit Resolve IDs, shared inventory policy,
    credential-aware cache manifests.

 -- Caio Barbieri <70986039+caiolombello@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0000
